            "validation_layers": [
              "RLP canonical form",
              "State trie validation"
            ],
            "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope",
            "notes": "Account encoding affects the state root. Non-canonical encoding produces a divergent state root."
          },
          "test_procedure": "1. Locate the encode_account function in the RLP codec implementation.\n2. Verify the function encodes account fields in the exact order: nonce, balance, storage_root, code_hash.\n3. Create test accounts with varying field values and encode them.\n4. Compare the resulting RLP bytes against known canonical encodings from reference implementations.\n5. Attempt to decode RLP with incorrect field ordering and verify rejection.\n6. Verify that state root computation uses only canonically-ordered RLP encodings.\n7. Test edge cases: zero values, maximum values, and empty code_hash scenarios.",
          "bug_class": "Input Validation",
          "risk_category": "Tampering",
          "notes": "Source: PROP-W5B6-50, Trust Boundary: tb-020, Assumption: asm-024"
        },
        "code_scope": {
          "locations": [],
          "resolution_status": "not_found",
          "resolution_error": "",
          "resolution_method": null
        }
      },
      "checklist_file": "outputs/02c_PARTIAL_W1B18_1771298989.json"
    },
