          "test_procedure": "1. Locate the parse_deposit_requests function in the codebase and identify the address comparison logic.\n2. Verify that the comparison uses exact equality (==) and not substring matching, prefix matching, or case-insensitive comparison.\n3. Confirm that DEPOSIT_CONTRACT_ADDRESS is a constant and cannot be modified at runtime.\n4. Deploy a malicious contract at a different address that emits logs with the same event signature as legitimate deposit events.\n5. Submit a transaction that triggers the malicious contract and verify that parse_deposit_requests rejects events from this non-canonical address.\n6. Test edge cases: addresses with similar prefixes/suffixes, zero address, and address with different checksums.",
          "bug_class": "Input Validation",
          "risk_category": "Spoofing",
          "notes": "Source: PROP-W5B6-51, Trust Boundary: tb-016, Threat: stride-spoofing-tb-016, Assumption: asm-017"
        },
        "code_scope": {
